# End Session

Verify the work and update project memory.

## Steps

1. Inspect changes:
   - `git status --short`
   - `git diff --stat`
2. Run relevant checks:
   - `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`
   - `{{LINT_COMMAND}}` if code style changed
   - `{{TYPECHECK_COMMAND}}` if typed code changed
3. Update `{{DOCS_PATH}}/ROADMAP.md`:
   - mark completed tasks
   - move finished items to `Done` if appropriate
   - add blockers or follow-up tasks
4. Prepend an entry to `{{DOCS_PATH}}/SESSION_LOG.md`:
   - feature
   - task
   - summary
   - files changed
   - decisions
   - tests/checks run
   - next step
5. Update `{{DOCS_PATH}}/LEARNED_PATTERNS.md`, `{{DOCS_PATH}}/OVERVIEW.md`, or `{{DOCS_PATH}}/ADR.md` only when the session changed durable knowledge.
6. Give the user a concise summary with verification results.

## Guardrails

- Do not commit, push, merge, or open a PR unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not hide failing checks. State exact commands and failure status.
